WEBVTT


00:00:28.248 --> 00:00:29.688
The question of happiness


00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:31.813
has preoccupied
philosophers, poets


00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.532
and pharmaceutical companies
for thousands of years.


00:00:35.688 --> 00:00:38.208
Clearly, it's a tricky one.


00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:41.128
When I graduated from
design school three years ago,


00:00:41.287 --> 00:00:44.015
I had a definite plan.


00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:47.768
Couple months at home,
put together a kickass portfolio,


00:00:47.927 --> 00:00:50.971
then I'd take Manhattan
by storm.


00:00:53.326 --> 00:00:54.887
And here is home.


00:00:55.887 --> 00:00:57.327
West Orange, New Jersey.


00:00:57.486 --> 00:00:59.091
Nice, huh?


00:01:00.687 --> 00:01:03.807
OK, it's not Manhattan,
but, like I say, it's temporary.


00:01:03.966 --> 00:01:07.730
I grew up here
with two families.


00:01:07.886 --> 00:01:10.570
That's my dad in blue,
and that's his best friend, Terry.


00:01:10.726 --> 00:01:12.570
The Inseparables.


00:01:12.726 --> 00:01:15.814
They go jogging together
three times a week without fail.


00:01:15.965 --> 00:01:18.126
You can set your clock by it.


00:01:18.285 --> 00:01:21.046
You could say life in the Oranges
is dependable.


00:01:21.205 --> 00:01:23.169
I can't believe
you made me do this.


00:01:23.325 --> 00:01:26.053
Good for your appetite.
See you in an hour.


00:01:26.205 --> 00:01:29.293
You can depend on Terry
to have a gadget for everything.


00:01:29.445 --> 00:01:32.172
Walked 1.2 miles.
Only stopped twice.


00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:33.645
That's great, honey.


00:01:33.804 --> 00:01:35.691
And you can
depend on Cathy


00:01:35.844 --> 00:01:37.644
to never hear
a single word he says.


00:01:37.804 --> 00:01:39.484
Make sure you put your bicycle
in the garage.


00:01:39.644 --> 00:01:41.488
And pull the pork
out of the freezer, honey.


00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:46.851
Across the street,
our house.


00:01:47.004 --> 00:01:49.371
Every year,
my mom gets more involved


00:01:49.524 --> 00:01:50.887
with her carolling group.


00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.844
They start rehearsing
in August.


00:01:53.003 --> 00:01:54.563
# Jingle bells
Jingle all the way... #


00:01:54.723 --> 00:01:57.288
And every year, my dad
hates them a little bit more.


00:02:00.323 --> 00:02:04.164
OK, sure. I'm still here.
I'm a few years behind in my plan.


00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:06.090
But you can't
rush these things.


00:02:06.243 --> 00:02:09.091
Portfolios need
to be perfect, right?


00:02:09.242 --> 00:02:11.882
Plus I have a day job
working in furniture, so...


00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:15.402
...as far as I was concerned,
everything was on track.


00:02:15.562 --> 00:02:18.606
# Happy birthday to you... #


00:02:18.761 --> 00:02:21.609
That is, until what
happened... happened


00:02:21.762 --> 00:02:23.846
Nina Ostroff.


00:02:24.001 --> 00:02:26.685
When all this started,
she was at a safe distance,


00:02:26.841 --> 00:02:28.881
3, 000 miles away
in San Francisco.


00:02:29.041 --> 00:02:32.685
I Happy birthday to you. I


00:02:32.841 --> 00:02:35.165
Make a wish, babe.


00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.808
And I was the fifth wheel


00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.208
to our parents'
regular Saturday foursome.


00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.040
Say it again.


00:02:49.199 --> 00:02:50.487
OK.


00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.963
Un coup de birch.


00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:54.603
Hey, Vanny.


00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.243
I read the most
interesting article


00:02:56.399 --> 00:02:58.167
called 'The IKEA Conspiracy',


00:02:58.319 --> 00:02:59.924
which you'd be
really fascinated by.


00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.400
- What it imagines is a...
- Terry?


00:03:01.559 --> 00:03:03.042
We need to call Nina.
We said 9:30.


00:03:03.199 --> 00:03:04.639
I'm on it.


00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:07.003
Vanessa, did you look at
that one-bedroom in Fort Lee?


00:03:07.158 --> 00:03:10.323
Yeah. It was, um, like a closet
in the basement.


00:03:10.478 --> 00:03:11.842
There's always something, honey.


00:03:11.998 --> 00:03:13.319
Don't be so choosy.
Nothing's perfect.


00:03:13.478 --> 00:03:15.639
There was, you know,
one window.


00:03:15.798 --> 00:03:17.642
- Paige, did I tell you...
- No room to breathe.


00:03:17.798 --> 00:03:19.478
...that Joan Marshack
was the listing agent on that?


00:03:19.638 --> 00:03:22.442
David, you are going
to really love this.


00:03:22.598 --> 00:03:27.399
This speaker box communicates
wirelessly with my cell phone.


00:03:27.558 --> 00:03:29.642
And guess where
I read about it first.


00:03:29.797 --> 00:03:31.805
'Consumer Reports'. Thank you
so much for the subscription.


00:03:31.958 --> 00:03:34.206
- I'm really enjoying it.
- You are consumingly welcome.


00:03:34.357 --> 00:03:37.445
I don't even have to take
my cell phone out of my pocket.


00:03:37.597 --> 00:03:38.918
Watch.


00:03:39.077 --> 00:03:40.921
Dial Nina.


00:03:41.077 --> 00:03:42.517
Please repeat request.


00:03:42.676 --> 00:03:43.997
Dial Nina.


00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.241
Maybe your pants
are blocking the signal.


00:03:46.396 --> 00:03:47.836
They're cotton.


00:03:49.276 --> 00:03:51.916
Nina's cell phone, dialling.


00:03:53.716 --> 00:03:56.717
Nina - their daughter
and my best friend


00:03:56.876 --> 00:03:58.884
from ages 0
to high school.


00:03:59.036 --> 00:04:01.436
We spent hours together
planning our big escape.


00:04:01.596 --> 00:04:03.560
I'm gonna live in New York.


00:04:03.715 --> 00:04:05.036
And Paris.


00:04:05.195 --> 00:04:07.443
And I'm gonna be a famous chef
and have a million lovers


00:04:07.595 --> 00:04:08.916
who'll take me
all over the world


00:04:09.075 --> 00:04:11.203
so I never have to come back
to New Jersey again.


00:04:11.355 --> 00:04:14.082
It's like
there's no air here, right?


00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:15.839
Totally.


00:04:18.514 --> 00:04:19.955
You'll come too, right?


00:04:20.114 --> 00:04:22.034
Are you kidding?


00:04:23.235 --> 00:04:25.002
Until sophomore year,


00:04:25.154 --> 00:04:29.442
when she abandoned me for
Liz Gaines and the Fun Bunch.


00:04:32.034 --> 00:04:36.234
She also kissed and later gave
a hand job to Peter Fortunate.


00:04:36.394 --> 00:04:39.514
I'd been secretly
in love with him forever.


00:04:40.633 --> 00:04:42.597
Then, just as her parents
were lining her up


00:04:42.753 --> 00:04:44.553
at some lame college
in Pennsylvania,


00:04:44.713 --> 00:04:47.157
she decided she was
going to travel the world.


00:04:47.313 --> 00:04:49.757
Or at least those parts


00:04:49.912 --> 00:04:51.832
that were out of
her mothefs cell phone range.


00:04:55.232 --> 00:04:56.879
Hello?


00:04:57.032 --> 00:04:59.432
Happy birthday, sweetie!


00:04:59.592 --> 00:05:01.240
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday, Nina.


00:05:01.392 --> 00:05:04.240
It's David and Paige.
Vanessa's here too.


00:05:04.392 --> 00:05:06.116
It's true. I'm here.


00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.560
Hey, Ethan.


00:05:07.711 --> 00:05:10.439
I think Nina's fucking parents
are on the phone.


00:05:12.192 --> 00:05:14.636
I didn't know I was having
a party. It was a surprise.


00:05:14.791 --> 00:05:16.875
Honey, we can't hear you.


00:05:17.031 --> 00:05:19.638
Ethan threw me
a surprise party.


00:05:19.791 --> 00:05:21.515
It's so great.


00:05:21.671 --> 00:05:22.992
Did you guys get
the pictures I sent?


00:05:23.151 --> 00:05:24.875
Yes, we did.


00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:26.711
More young men should have earrings
