...most of the play, being
a big movie producer and all.


00:13:40.921 --> 00:13:43.169
Finally!


00:13:45.601 --> 00:13:47.729
Where there's dessert,
there's hope.


00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:55.121
Your mom told me about what
happened with that Ethan guy.


00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:57.200
You OK?


00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:02.000
Yeah.


00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.288
I'm good, thanks.


00:14:05.599 --> 00:14:07.519
So, what about you?


00:14:07.679 --> 00:14:09.688
How's the liquor
advertising business going?


00:14:09.839 --> 00:14:11.607
Still pushing booze
onto minors?


00:14:11.759 --> 00:14:14.203
Yes, I am.


00:14:14.359 --> 00:14:15.679
Actually,
I just got a promotion.


00:14:15.839 --> 00:14:17.366
I'm now executive
vice-president,


00:14:17.519 --> 00:14:18.839
creative accounts.


00:14:18.998 --> 00:14:20.526
Congratulations.


00:14:20.679 --> 00:14:22.807
Was that something
you wanted?


00:14:22.958 --> 00:14:24.999
Not really.


00:14:25.158 --> 00:14:27.078
You want me to spoon this
onto the plates?


00:14:27.238 --> 00:14:28.722
Please.


00:14:28.878 --> 00:14:32.359
Uh... Don't just eat it
right out the carton.


00:14:35.078 --> 00:14:37.958
Is it good?


00:14:40.157 --> 00:14:41.565
- It's cold.
- What?


00:14:41.718 --> 00:14:45.722
Hey. I brought that ice-cream
for the pies.


00:14:45.877 --> 00:14:47.764
He made me eat it.


00:14:48.997 --> 00:14:50.765
Well, Cathy wants
to serve dessert.


00:14:50.917 --> 00:14:52.685
Will you please
bring in some plates?


00:14:54.956 --> 00:14:57.324
I still need Christmas lists
from everyone by tonight.


00:14:57.477 --> 00:14:58.797
I'm leaving early tomorrow.


00:14:58.956 --> 00:15:00.964
- Black Friday.
- Don't make fun.


00:15:01.116 --> 00:15:04.924
Last year, I got there at 3am
and I was still 210 in line.


00:15:05.076 --> 00:15:06.516
Why would anyone
want to shop


00:15:06.676 --> 00:15:08.281
on the same day
as everyone else?


00:15:08.436 --> 00:15:10.356
I hear that
they have fist fights


00:15:10.516 --> 00:15:12.240
and people throw their children
at each other.


00:15:12.396 --> 00:15:15.244
Terry! No.
It's really a very...


00:15:15.395 --> 00:15:19.279
Very communal, Christmassy
experience. It's beautiful.


00:15:19.435 --> 00:15:20.799
Listen, I know it's late,


00:15:20.955 --> 00:15:22.439
but I think
we should have a toast.


00:15:22.595 --> 00:15:24.963
It's Thanksgiving. We have
so much to be thankful for.


00:15:25.115 --> 00:15:27.275
Toby is going to China.


00:15:27.434 --> 00:15:28.755
Very exciting.


00:15:28.915 --> 00:15:31.479
Nina is finally
back at home.


00:15:31.635 --> 00:15:34.396
And Vanessa
continues to live among us,


00:15:34.554 --> 00:15:36.234
bringing us joy every day.


00:15:36.394 --> 00:15:38.281
To the Walling
and Ostroff clans.


00:15:38.434 --> 00:15:42.002
Who knew that two families
could get this close?


00:15:42.154 --> 00:15:43.474
Hear, hear.


00:15:43.633 --> 00:15:46.198
I still think we could be
a little closer.


00:15:48.193 --> 00:15:50.474
Well said.


00:15:52.513 --> 00:15:55.601
Man, I thought your mom
was going to applaud


00:15:55.753 --> 00:15:57.074
when she saw us
leave together.


00:15:57.233 --> 00:16:00.081
The woman
is a total lunatic.


00:16:00.233 --> 00:16:02.077
In the first three years
I was gone,


00:16:02.233 --> 00:16:04.033
she sent me
letters from the cat.


00:16:04.192 --> 00:16:06.440
"Dear Nina,
Don't be difficult.


00:16:06.593 --> 00:16:08.000
"Call your mother
on her birthday."


00:16:08.152 --> 00:16:10.520
That's great, actually.
I kind of like that.


00:16:10.672 --> 00:16:13.160
Now you understand
why I never came back.


00:16:14.192 --> 00:16:16.275
Yeah. No, I hear ya. But...


00:16:16.432 --> 00:16:18.952
I'm glad you did.


00:16:20.271 --> 00:16:21.319
Shut up.


00:16:25.471 --> 00:16:27.195
Dance with me.


00:16:28.831 --> 00:16:30.315
Totally.


00:16:33.991 --> 00:16:35.551
You OK?


00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:37.031
I need to get some water.


00:16:37.191 --> 00:16:39.078
- Can I get some water?
- OK. Sit down, wild man.


00:16:39.231 --> 00:16:42.712
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.


00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.554
- Hey.
- Toby needs water.


00:16:49.709 --> 00:16:51.477
What are you doing up?


00:16:51.629 --> 00:16:54.837
Just watching a little TV
in the man cave.


00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:58.110
- Man cave?
- It's the pool house.


00:16:58.269 --> 00:17:01.030
I got one of those
worldwide sports...


00:17:01.189 --> 00:17:03.317
...something something package
your dad recommended.


00:17:03.469 --> 00:17:05.673
There's this
Korean basketball league


00:17:05.829 --> 00:17:07.476
which is completely crazy.


00:17:07.629 --> 00:17:09.757
You know, it's not good
to eat peanut butter


00:17:09.908 --> 00:17:11.229
this late at night.


00:17:11.388 --> 00:17:12.709
It'll make you fat.


00:17:12.868 --> 00:17:14.712
I'm not fat.


00:17:14.868 --> 00:17:16.593
You will be if you
keep eating like that


00:17:16.748 --> 00:17:18.068
at 2:00 in the morning.


00:17:18.228 --> 00:17:19.875
And where'd you pick
this little factoid up?


00:17:20.028 --> 00:17:21.632
I worked in
a lot of restaurants.


00:17:21.787 --> 00:17:23.915
Restaurants
that serve peanut butter?


00:17:24.068 --> 00:17:26.076
Look, do whatever you want.


00:17:26.228 --> 00:17:28.672
I'm just saying
that you wouldn't look good fat.


00:17:31.147 --> 00:17:33.034
I should get back downstairs.


00:17:33.187 --> 00:17:34.954
Yeah, make your mother
very happy. You know that.


00:17:35.107 --> 00:17:36.427
It's what I live for.


00:18:23.824 --> 00:18:25.744
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:18:26.944 --> 00:18:28.471
What happened to Toby?


00:18:28.624 --> 00:18:30.544
I cut him up
in little pieces


00:18:30.704 --> 00:18:32.504
and put him in the fridge
for later.


00:18:39.703 --> 00:18:41.263
Who's playing?


00:18:42.863 --> 00:18:44.707
I have no idea.


00:18:44.863 --> 00:18:46.707
It's...it's the, um...


00:18:49.063 --> 00:18:51.146
...guys in red against the...
the guys in white.


00:18:51.303 --> 00:18:52.950
- White. I got it.
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:18:53.103 --> 00:18:55.111
Go, reds.


00:18:55.262 --> 00:18:56.943
Or White.


00:18:57.102 --> 00:18:58.782
You know.


00:19:42.499 --> 00:19:44.507
Oh, fuck.


00:19:47.499 --> 00:19:50.827
One bedroom, high ceilings.
Close to the PATH train.


00:19:50.979 --> 00:19:52.779
Ooh, washer dryer.


00:19:52.939 --> 00:19:55.503
- Plus it's crazy bright.
- Yeah.


00:19:55.658 --> 00:19:58.223
Well, that's morning light.


00:19:58.379 --> 00:20:00.223
I don't want that.


00:20:00.378 --> 00:20:03.227
Wow, that's, like,
your best excuse in two weeks.


00:20:03.378 --> 00:20:04.938
Hello, Koosers.


00:20:05.099 --> 00:20:07.018
- Did you sell that dresser?
- I did not.


00:20:07.178 --> 00:20:08.618
She's not interested
in the apartment, Henry.


00:20:08.778 --> 00:20:10.099
I told you.


00:20:10.258 --> 00:20:11.786
What?


00:20:11.938 --> 00:20:13.542
What do you mean,
"I told you"?


00:20:13.698 --> 00:20:16.382
You've been talking about
moving out for two years.


00:20:16.537 --> 00:20:18.305
You know what?
I'm saving money. Alright?


00:20:18.457 --> 00:20:20.465
I have a very definite plan.


00:20:20.617 --> 00:20:22.821
You mean that "stay at home,
corrode your soul" plan?


00:20:22.977 --> 00:20:24.941
No, no - the plan
where I move to the city


00:20:25.097 --> 00:20:26.581
and I work with
a big designer.


00:20:26.737 --> 00:20:28.865
I've already made
serious contacts.


00:20:29.017 --> 00:20:30.861
From where'?


00:20:31.017 --> 00:20:36.298
Huffman Koos? Well, you know me
and her and Marlon.


00:20:36.456 --> 00:20:39.141
Hey, I'm serious.
We're worried about you.


00:20:39.296 --> 00:20:41.456
OK, thank you.
I got it under control.


00:20:41.616 --> 00:20:43.143
You guys
go worry about yourselves.


00:20:46.096 --> 00:20:47.896
Wow. There she is'


00:20:48.055 --> 00:20:51.263
1 pm. Very impressive.


00:20:51.416 --> 00:20:53.696
So? Did you have fun
last night?


00:20:53.855 --> 00:20:55.535
I'm sure you'd love
a full report.


00:20:55.695 --> 00:20:57.704
You know,
some mothers and daughters


00:20:57.855 --> 00:21:00.495
actually talk about
these things, like friends.


00:21:00.654 --> 00:21:02.782
It's not happening.


00:21:02.935 --> 00:21:06.743
Well, maybe Toby will be
better company than you.


00:21:06.894 --> 00:21:08.302
Hi!


00:21:14.694 --> 00:21:16.418
Try and control yourself.


00:21:21.093 --> 00:21:22.337
Hey, Nina.


00:21:22.493 --> 00:21:25.537
- Morning, Cathy.
- Good morning, Tobias.


00:21:25.693 --> 00:21:28.334
- Uh, you forgot your sweater.
- Thank you.


00:21:28.493 --> 00:21:30.293
Can I get you
some breakfast, honey?


00:21:30.453 --> 00:21:32.657
No, thanks. I'm OK. Thanks.


00:21:34.132 --> 00:21:36.141
Well, I'll give you two
some privacy.


00:21:36.293 --> 00:21:39.020
There you are.


00:21:42.333 --> 00:21:44.133
I can hear you
hovering out there!


00:21:44.292 --> 00:21:45.820
Fine.


00:21:47.132 --> 00:21:48.813
You're looking a little crispy
this morning.


00:21:48.972 --> 00:21:51.013
Oh, thank you.
You can really put 'em away.


00:21:51.172 --> 00:21:53.933
Did I, uh...
Did I pass out?


00:21:54.092 --> 00:21:55.936
Yeah. Mmm, pretty much.


00:21:56.091 --> 00:21:58.295
Sorry about that.


00:21:58.451 --> 00:22:00.972
- No.
- Um...


00:22:02.131 --> 00:22:03.931
Look.
Uh, I was thinking.


00:22:04.091 --> 00:22:08.500
I had a really fun time last night
before passing out, and...


00:22:08.651 --> 00:22:10.779
...I'm supposed to have dinner
with my folks tonight.


00:22:10.931 --> 00:22:13.615
And being as
I'm leaving in two days,


00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:18.331
I thought, you know,
maybe you'd like to join us


00:22:18.490 --> 00:22:20.618
so we could
hang out more.


00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:25.734
Yeah. Dinner with you and
your parents, it...sounds great.


00:22:30.769 --> 00:22:32.973
- Come on, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:34.809 --> 00:22:36.457
Alright. OK.


00:22:36.609 --> 00:22:38.529
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:38.689 --> 00:22:42.378
Toby, it's called
the fast-moving tile game.


00:22:42.529 --> 00:22:44.449
Hold.


00:22:47.289 --> 00:22:49.176
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold!


00:22:49.328 --> 00:22:51.696
OK. OK.


00:22:51.849 --> 00:22:53.496
Actually,
just go out ahead of me.


00:22:53.648 --> 00:22:55.372
Oh!


00:22:55.528 --> 00:22:58.048
5, the 13. I'm out!


00:22:58.208 --> 00:23:00.815
- What?
- Ah. Yes.


00:23:00.968 --> 00:23:02.528
Now, who's gonna help me
with the dishes?


00:23:02.688 --> 00:23:04.171
I will, Mom. Wait.


00:23:04.328 --> 00:23:06.248
Hang on a sec.
I gotta take this. It's work.


00:23:06.407 --> 00:23:07.967
This is Toby.


00:23:08.127 --> 00:23:09.611
Oh, hello, sir.


00:23:09.767 --> 00:23:11.088
Uh-huh.


00:23:11.247 --> 00:23:12.567
- No, no, it's no problem.
- Yeah.


00:23:12.727 --> 00:23:14.407
I think maybe
I'll go pick up a movie


00:23:14.567 --> 00:23:16.050
in case you want to
watch something later.


00:23:16.207 --> 00:23:19.011
- That sounds fun.
- I'll come with you.


00:23:19.166 --> 00:23:21.774
Keep you company
while Toby does the dishes.


00:23:32.366 --> 00:23:33.729
Look.


00:23:33.886 --> 00:23:36.929
What happened last night
was a mistake.


00:23:37.086 --> 00:23:39.334
- OK?
- No, you're right.


00:23:42.085 --> 00:23:45.250
Relax, OK?
It was nothing.


00:23:45.405 --> 00:23:47.609
And you stopped it.
You're absolved.


00:23:57.924 --> 00:23:59.572
Hello in there?


00:23:59.724 --> 00:24:01.285
Is there anyone in there?


00:24:01.444 --> 00:24:04.368
You just have to
instigate trouble.


00:24:04.524 --> 00:24:07.328
I do not instigate trouble.


00:24:07.484 --> 00:24:08.804
Well, OK.


00:24:08.963 --> 00:24:10.491
Well, then, Why'd you
come to dinner tonight?


00:24:10.643 --> 00:24:11.964
Toby invited me.


00:24:12.123 --> 00:24:13.891
And now that we're
talking about instigators,


00:24:14.043 --> 00:24:15.887
you leaned into me.


00:24:16.043 --> 00:24:17.604
I leaned into you?


00:24:17.763 --> 00:24:19.607
- I leaned... I did not lean.
- Yes, you did.


00:24:19.763 --> 00:24:21.324
- You leaned into me.
- What?!


00:24:21.483 --> 00:24:23.491
Oh... He said, she said.


00:24:25.162 --> 00:24:26.483
He said, she said.


00:24:26.642 --> 00:24:28.322
Where did that come from?


00:24:28.482 --> 00:24:30.402
I have no idea
where that came from.


00:24:36.602 --> 00:24:38.446
I'm not instigating.


00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:05.244
I've been thinking
about getting


00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:07.409
one of those
giant electric snow globes.


00:25:07.560 --> 00:25:10.604
You ever seen one of those?
Really big ones?


00:25:10.760 --> 00:25:12.768
Fantastic.


00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:14.884
Mom?


00:25:15.039 --> 00:25:17.123
We're in here, honey.


00:25:17.279 --> 00:25:19.767
I'm going out.


00:25:19.919 --> 00:25:22.003
Well!


00:25:22.160 --> 00:25:24.680
Well, don't you look nice?


00:25:24.839 --> 00:25:26.367
Thanks.


00:25:26.519 --> 00:25:27.960
So is Toby
taking you somewhere?


00:25:28.119 --> 00:25:30.880
- Uh, yeah.
- OK. OK.


00:25:31.039 --> 00:25:32.403
- Fine.
- Mom!


00:25:32.559 --> 00:25:34.283
Give me some room.


00:25:34.438 --> 00:25:36.719
Fine. Have fun.


00:25:40.638 --> 00:25:42.243
Is she eating with us?


00:25:42.398 --> 00:25:45.279
Toby is taking her out.
She was all dressed up.


00:25:45.438 --> 00:25:47.162
- Toby already left for DC.
- What?


00:25:47.318 --> 00:25:48.725
Yeah, first thing
this morning.


00:25:48.878 --> 00:25:50.722
Some congressman wanted
to be with the delegation


00:25:50.877 --> 00:25:52.438
before they went to China.


00:26:21.916 --> 00:26:24.916
"Left this morning."
Oh, shit!


00:26:37.074 --> 00:26:39.158
- H-hello?
- Mom?


00:26:39.315 --> 00:26:41.323
Listen. I lied earlier.


00:26:41.474 --> 00:26:43.242
I'm not going out with Toby.


00:26:43.394 --> 00:26:45.118
He actually left for Washington
this morning.


00:26:45.274 --> 00:26:48.001
- Oh?
- Yeah.


00:26:48.154 --> 00:26:52.321
I'm meeting Meredith Lovett.
Remember her?


00:26:52.474 --> 00:26:54.797
I didn't tell you because
I know you don't like her.


00:26:54.954 --> 00:26:59.002
Oh, honey, thank you.
Thank you for telling me.


00:26:59.153 --> 00:27:02.961
You know...
You don't have to lie to me.


00:27:03.113 --> 00:27:05.154
I know.


00:27:05.313 --> 00:27:07.037
So where are you going?


00:27:08.633 --> 00:27:11.841
Uh, we're going to the Regal
to see a movie.


00:27:13.832 --> 00:27:15.153
Uh, Mom?


00:27:15.312 --> 00:27:17.832
Thanks...for being so cool


00:27:17.992 --> 00:27:20.240
and letting me come back
and stay and everything.


00:27:20.392 --> 00:27:23.240
I've been feeling really
tossed around lately, so...


00:27:23.391 --> 00:27:26.796
You know.
Thanks for being there.


00:27:28.272 --> 00:27:30.672
OK, well...
I'll see you later for dinner.


00:27:35.631 --> 00:27:37.191
Oh, my...


00:28:14.029 --> 00:28:15.273
Whoa!


00:28:15.429 --> 00:28:17.470
Cathy.


00:28:17.629 --> 00:28:19.832
- What are you...?
- I'm, uh...


00:28:19.989 --> 00:28:22.433
- What are you...
- I'm not, uh... Nothing.


00:28:22.589 --> 00:28:26.113
Paige and I had a fight,
and I spent the night here. So...


00:28:28.028 --> 00:28:30.472
Oh, my God!


00:28:30.628 --> 00:28:32.232
Hey, Nina.


00:28:32.387 --> 00:28:33.828
- What are you...
- Oh, my God!


00:28:33.988 --> 00:28:35.428
Cathy! Slow down.


00:28:35.588 --> 00:28:38.795
Slow down? I can read
an ice bucket, David.


00:28:38.948 --> 00:28:40.989
- Cathy.
- Oh, my God!


00:28:41.147 --> 00:28:43.995
I'm gonna throw up!


00:28:49.106 --> 00:28:51.627
- Jesus, David!
- Paige, listen to me.


00:28:51.787 --> 00:28:53.707
Just tell me how long
it's been going on.


00:28:53.867 --> 00:28:56.027
We kissed. That's it.


00:28:56.187 --> 00:28:58.631
Then what the hell were you
doing in a goddamn motel room?


00:28:58.786 --> 00:29:00.434
This...


00:29:02.186 --> 00:29:04.706
I'm sorry.
The whole thing was wrong.


00:29:04.866 --> 00:29:06.187
But let's be honest.


00:29:06.346 --> 00:29:08.430
Things have not been good
between us for a long time.


00:29:08.585 --> 00:29:10.069
Oh, God, don't do that.


00:29:10.225 --> 00:29:12.625
Don't apologise and then
blame me in the same sentence.


00:29:12.786 --> 00:29:14.794
Come on, Paige.
You're not happy either.


00:29:14.945 --> 00:29:17.346
It's not about
being happy, David!


00:29:17.505 --> 00:29:19.425
Well, then, what is it?


00:29:38.984 --> 00:29:40.752
Jesus, say something already.


00:29:40.904 --> 00:29:42.868
I will say something
when I want.


00:29:43.023 --> 00:29:45.424
You don't get to decide
when I say something. I decide!


00:29:45.584 --> 00:29:48.028
- Then decide already!
- I'll decide.


00:29:48.184 --> 00:29:51.468
You have caused
some serious trouble


00:29:51.624 --> 00:29:52.911
in the past, young lady.


00:29:53.063 --> 00:29:54.471
Don't you
roll your eyes at me.


00:29:54.623 --> 00:29:56.587
I'm sorry, it doesn't work
when you try to play


00:29:56.743 --> 00:29:58.467
the stern father - it looks like
you're pretending.


00:29:58.623 --> 00:30:00.707
Your father is not pretending!
We are furious!


00:30:00.862 --> 00:30:02.270
I'm not pretending.


00:30:02.423 --> 00:30:03.983
David and I,
we like each other.


00:30:04.142 --> 00:30:06.390
- Oh, my God.
- We've always been close.


00:30:06.542 --> 00:30:08.583
It's not like we planned this.
It just happened.


00:30:08.742 --> 00:30:10.347
- You like each other?
- Yeah.


00:30:10.502 --> 00:30:11.823
- Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God!


00:30:11.982 --> 00:30:14.502
I know what this is -
