00:45:04.329 --> 00:45:06.609
he went online and found
a pick-up ultimate frisbee game


00:45:06.768 --> 00:45:08.132
in Paramus.


00:45:08.288 --> 00:45:11.332
Hey, guys! You, uh...
you got room for one more?


00:45:11.488 --> 00:45:13.572
No daylight. No daylight.


00:45:13.728 --> 00:45:18.528
So it was really Jared Kass
and I, and Joel Silver...


00:45:18.688 --> 00:45:20.368
Joel Silver,
the movie producer?


00:45:20.528 --> 00:45:21.772
Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:22.848 --> 00:45:24.331
My mother
had been making herself


00:45:24.487 --> 00:45:26.168
mysteriously unavailable.


00:45:27.327 --> 00:45:29.531
But, as all our neighbours
discovered...


00:45:31.127 --> 00:45:34.292
...she hadn't completely lost sight
of the Christmas spirit.


00:45:39.487 --> 00:45:40.895
Terry!


00:45:41.046 --> 00:45:42.726
Everything was changing.


00:45:42.887 --> 00:45:44.207
Terry!


00:45:44.366 --> 00:45:45.971
No-one even recognised
each other anymore.


00:45:48.806 --> 00:45:51.567
- Smoothie?
- Oh, good God.


00:45:54.646 --> 00:45:56.686
Very good.


00:45:56.846 --> 00:45:58.929
Now kiss the chef.


00:46:10.725 --> 00:46:12.733
Maybe they are
really in love.


00:46:12.885 --> 00:46:14.205
You said it doesn't last.


00:46:14.364 --> 00:46:16.645
You said that the grasses only
wanted the cows for their money.


00:46:16.805 --> 00:46:18.365
Usually that is the case,
but not always.


00:46:18.524 --> 00:46:20.532
- Your dad is pretty cute.
- Don't be gross, OK?


00:46:20.684 --> 00:46:22.528
Just because you haven't gotten
laid in, like, three weeks.


00:46:22.684 --> 00:46:24.648
Perhaps your problem is
more with Nina than your father.


00:46:24.804 --> 00:46:26.571
Oh, is that so, Henry?
Why is that?


00:46:26.724 --> 00:46:28.044
Because maybe
you are jealous,


00:46:28.203 --> 00:46:31.444
because she has travelled
many places and has lived,


00:46:31.604 --> 00:46:34.365
because she takes chances.


00:46:34.523 --> 00:46:35.844
No. You know what?


00:46:36.004 --> 00:46:37.531
You, my friend,
have breathed in


00:46:37.683 --> 00:46:39.527
a little too much
of this cheap pine wax, OK?


00:46:39.683 --> 00:46:42.564
'Cause she's a selfish skank.
And he's selfish too.


00:46:42.723 --> 00:46:45.004
Yeah, but if he
really is happier with her


00:46:45.163 --> 00:46:46.527
and you make him stop,


00:46:46.683 --> 00:46:48.243
then you're the one
who's being selfish.


00:46:50.083 --> 00:46:51.763
That is maybe
the most intelligent thing


00:46:51.922 --> 00:46:53.362
you have ever said.


00:47:09.001 --> 00:47:10.769
Hey.


00:47:10.921 --> 00:47:13.769
What is
Barnyard International?


00:47:13.921 --> 00:47:16.922
Well, um... See those presents
you got at babyGap?


00:47:17.081 --> 00:47:19.209
Instead of giving those
to a baby


00:47:19.360 --> 00:47:20.921
who might already
have lots of clothes,


00:47:21.081 --> 00:47:23.001
why not help a baby
who doesn't have any food?


00:47:23.161 --> 00:47:24.481
They're not for a baby.


00:47:24.640 --> 00:47:26.081
They're for my husband's
new girlfriend.


00:47:28.200 --> 00:47:29.684
Here's some pamphlets.


00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:34.564
"One goat
can provide a family


00:47:34.719 --> 00:47:36.847
"with enough milk
for an entire year."


00:47:38.640 --> 00:47:40.768
It's like the Christmas gift
that keeps giving.


00:47:40.919 --> 00:47:42.479
Yeah. It is.


00:47:42.640 --> 00:47:44.560
That's good. Can I use that?


00:47:44.719 --> 00:47:47.163
Sure.


00:47:54.519 --> 00:47:56.766
Oh, yes! Oh! Oh!


00:48:04.478 --> 00:48:07.478
There are gift receipts inside,
if anyone wants to return them.


00:48:11.118 --> 00:48:12.842
I think after Christmas Eve,


00:48:12.997 --> 00:48:15.442
we should demand
that Paige have dinner with us.


00:48:18.397 --> 00:48:20.077
What are you doing?


00:48:20.237 --> 00:48:21.884
Come here.


00:48:24.037 --> 00:48:26.437
- I have toothpaste in my mouth.
- I don't care.


00:48:31.636 --> 00:48:33.360
Come here.


00:48:44.036 --> 00:48:47.080
OK. Thank you
for dropping me off.


00:48:47.236 --> 00:48:49.277
I got you these.


00:48:54.355 --> 00:48:56.155
Chef's clogs.


00:48:56.315 --> 00:48:58.202
You said after working last night,
your feet hurt, so...


00:48:58.354 --> 00:49:00.034
You're so sweet.


00:49:08.674 --> 00:49:10.518
OK. You're gonna
make me late.


00:49:10.674 --> 00:49:12.474
Whoo!


00:49:22.233 --> 00:49:23.553
- That was fast.
- Yeah.


00:49:23.714 --> 00:49:25.874
Um...


00:49:26.033 --> 00:49:27.517
What?


00:49:29.673 --> 00:49:30.993
Nothing.


00:49:31.152 --> 00:49:32.473
What's up?


00:49:32.633 --> 00:49:33.954
Nothing.


00:49:34.113 --> 00:49:35.717
Come on.
Tell me what's wrong.


00:49:37.632 --> 00:49:39.913
- I...
- I love you, Nina.


00:49:41.872 --> 00:49:45.353
You shit. You suck.
I wanted to say it first.


00:49:47.112 --> 00:49:49.873
Well, now I'm not saying it.
You blew it, buddy.


00:49:51.871 --> 00:49:54.075
I'm just kidding.
I love you too.


00:49:58.991 --> 00:50:01.631
You guys were married
for 28 years.


00:50:01.791 --> 00:50:04.039
If anyone should call,
it should be him.


00:50:04.190 --> 00:50:06.231
- Do you have any perfume?
- No.


00:50:06.390 --> 00:50:09.075
What?! Where are you
even going?


00:50:09.231 --> 00:50:11.631
Well, I read about
a late-evening cabaret show


00:50:11.790 --> 00:50:13.274
that begins at 9:30.


00:50:13.430 --> 00:50:15.678
- I'm taking myself out.
- Cabaret?


00:50:15.831 --> 00:50:17.959
Am I the only one
who's dealing with this?


00:50:18.110 --> 00:50:21.711
I mean, don't you
want to come back home?


00:50:23.669 --> 00:50:25.110
I'm not sure.


00:50:25.270 --> 00:50:27.790
I'm having a good time
for once.


00:50:27.949 --> 00:50:31.877
I'd like to see you
do the same.


00:50:35.469 --> 00:50:36.996
Let's go, guys!
Pick up the pace!


00:50:37.149 --> 00:50:38.829
Hey, Mondo!
Where's my rigatoni? Let's go!


00:50:38.989 --> 00:50:40.473
Bring it up, parmigiana.


00:50:40.629 --> 00:50:42.429
Nina! Plate 27!


00:50:42.588 --> 00:50:43.952
Alright, guys-


00:50:44.108 --> 00:50:46.432
On 24, I got a mahi mahi
and a chicken parmigiana.


00:50:46.588 --> 00:50:48.475
Thanks for sending her to me.
She's a good worker.


00:50:48.628 --> 00:50:50.036
- Well, that's great.
- Chef likes her.


00:50:50.188 --> 00:50:53.353
Haven't seen you and Paige
for a while. It's good to see you.


00:50:53.508 --> 00:50:55.953
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


00:51:24.866 --> 00:51:27.790
- Done with your appetiser, sir?
- Sorry?


00:51:27.946 --> 00:51:29.474
Done with
your appetiser, sir?


00:51:29.625 --> 00:51:31.589
Yeah. That... Yeah.
That's great. Thanks.


00:51:36.306 --> 00:51:37.833
Hello.


00:51:39.145 --> 00:51:40.673
Hi, Paige.


00:51:42.665 --> 00:51:45.152
Nice move
on the Christmas card.


00:51:45.305 --> 00:51:46.952
Thank you.


00:51:47.985 --> 00:51:51.106
- Dining alone?
- Uh, yeah. I guess.


00:51:52.424 --> 00:51:54.268
So how are you doing?
Is everything...


00:51:54.425 --> 00:51:56.225
Sit down. Don't have to
make this uncomfortable.


00:51:56.384 --> 00:51:57.867
Just...


00:52:00.504 --> 00:52:02.752
Plus, you know
how I hate pleasantries.


00:52:04.264 --> 00:52:06.348
What about you?


00:52:06.503 --> 00:52:08.511
You look happy.


00:52:09.904 --> 00:52:11.464
Things are OK.
You know, I'm...


00:52:11.623 --> 00:52:14.068
If you're happy,
you can say so.


00:52:14.223 --> 00:52:15.990
You don't need
to spare my feelings.


00:52:16.143 --> 00:52:20.027
Just...be genuine,
David, please.


00:52:20.183 --> 00:52:21.787
Please.


00:52:24.183 --> 00:52:26.343
Yes. I'm happy-


00:52:29.742 --> 00:52:31.302
Thank you.


00:52:31.462 --> 00:52:33.022
Yeah.


00:52:34.422 --> 00:52:36.342
Look, I know
there's nothing I can say...


00:52:36.502 --> 00:52:37.910
Then don't try.


00:52:38.061 --> 00:52:39.861
Paige, stop. Please.


00:52:40.021 --> 00:52:42.269
This is exactly
how we got to this.


00:52:43.662 --> 00:52:48.103
OK, not exactly.
It's partly.


00:52:48.261 --> 00:52:51.109
We stopped talking
to each other.


00:52:53.461 --> 00:52:56.025
I used to love who I was
around you.


00:52:56.180 --> 00:52:58.908
What happened to us?


00:53:00.460 --> 00:53:02.948
We used to have fun.
Remember that?


00:53:04.900 --> 00:53:07.421
We used to laugh.
God, you were so funny.


00:53:07.580 --> 00:53:09.227
I'm still funny.


00:53:09.380 --> 00:53:11.464
I'm... Ask them.


00:53:33.419 --> 00:53:35.186
Shelly just fired me!


00:53:35.339 --> 00:53:36.866
Hey, hey.


00:53:37.018 --> 00:53:40.345
- What happened?
- Oh! This is fucking bullshit!


00:53:40.498 --> 00:53:43.062
- What? Why?
- Because he's not an idiot.


00:53:43.218 --> 00:53:45.978
He saw you and Paige, and he
saw me, and he figured it out.


00:53:46.138 --> 00:53:48.461
He said he didn't want
to be in the middle of it.


00:53:48.618 --> 00:53:50.626
And I was good at that job!


00:53:50.777 --> 00:53:52.741
Why...


00:53:52.898 --> 00:53:55.178
Why were you talking to her?


00:53:55.337 --> 00:53:57.017
She came into the restaurant.


00:53:57.176 --> 00:53:59.937
What do you expect me to do?


00:54:00.097 --> 00:54:02.420
I saw you sitting with her,
and I just thought...


00:54:04.977 --> 00:54:06.297
Thought what?


00:54:06.457 --> 00:54:08.224
I don't know.


00:54:10.696 --> 00:54:12.584
You looked normal together.


00:54:19.815 --> 00:54:22.423
Can we please get out of here?


00:54:30.494 --> 00:54:31.858
# I really can't stay


00:54:32.014 --> 00:54:33.814
# But, baby,
it's cold outside


00:54:33.975 --> 00:54:36.855
- # I've got to go away
- # But, baby, it's cold outside


00:54:37.015 --> 00:54:38.619
# This evening has been...


00:54:38.774 --> 00:54:40.302
# Been hoping
that you drop in


00:54:40.454 --> 00:54:41.818
# So very nice


00:54:41.974 --> 00:54:45.018
# I'll hold your hands
They're just like ice


00:54:45.174 --> 00:54:46.974
# My mother
will start to worry... I


00:54:47.134 --> 00:54:48.901
Hi. Mrs Ostroff'?


00:54:49.054 --> 00:54:50.701
We've never met.


00:54:50.854 --> 00:54:52.982
But I'm Ethan.


00:54:57.774 --> 00:54:59.498
You're our leader.
You can't quit!


00:54:59.653 --> 00:55:02.894
Christmas Eve is in, like,
six days. They're counting on us.


00:55:03.053 --> 00:55:07.221
Try and calm down. Calm down.


00:55:07.373 --> 00:55:10.254
Calm down. Order!


00:55:10.412 --> 00:55:12.299
I know you're upset.


00:55:12.453 --> 00:55:16.021
But you're all
dedicated and talented singers.


00:55:17.492 --> 00:55:18.813
Marcus will take over
as leader.


00:55:18.972 --> 00:55:21.296
- What?!
- Marcus?


00:55:21.452 --> 00:55:23.416
- Why are you even doing this?
- Yeah.


00:55:23.571 --> 00:55:27.215
Well, I believe these pamphlets
should explain everything.


00:55:27.372 --> 00:55:30.056
Each cow or goat
will allow its recipient


00:55:30.211 --> 00:55:32.819
independence
and self-sufficiency


00:55:32.971 --> 00:55:35.252
for years to come.


00:55:36.251 --> 00:55:38.455
And that's pretty great,
isn't it?


00:55:39.771 --> 00:55:42.619
Shelly, this has
nothing to do with you.


00:55:42.770 --> 00:55:44.614
No, I know it's complicated.


00:55:44.771 --> 00:55:46.855
No. I understand.


00:55:48.290 --> 00:55:50.058
Thanks for calling back.


00:55:52.890 --> 00:55:54.211
Told you.


00:55:54.370 --> 00:55:56.094
He'll write you
a reference, but...


00:55:56.250 --> 00:55:57.854
Yeah. He doesn't
want to get involved.


00:55:58.009 --> 00:56:01.491
This isn't gonna work.
I need to find another job.


00:56:01.650 --> 00:56:03.330
I can't stay at Meredith's
rent-free.


00:56:03.489 --> 00:56:04.810
I know.


00:56:04.970 --> 00:56:06.290
And I can't stay here,


00:56:06.449 --> 00:56:07.857
across the street
from my parents.


00:56:08.009 --> 00:56:10.770
- I love you. But...
- What the fuck?


00:56:10.929 --> 00:56:14.333
- Ethan?
- What the hell is going on?


00:56:14.489 --> 00:56:17.577
- What are you doing here?
- Ethan? Like, Ethan Ethan?


00:56:17.729 --> 00:56:20.610
- How did you get in here?
- Your mom gave me the keys.


00:56:20.768 --> 00:56:22.416
She told me
to let myself in,


00:56:22.568 --> 00:56:24.096
like you might not
hear the bell.


00:56:24.248 --> 00:56:26.768
Look, Ethan, I'm sorry, but I'm
gonna have to ask you to leave.


00:56:26.928 --> 00:56:30.332
You can ask, but I'm not gonna.
Who is this?


00:56:30.487 --> 00:56:32.375
Ethan, this is David -
David and Paige,


00:56:32.528 --> 00:56:34.492
my parents' best friends
from across the street.


00:56:35.727 --> 00:56:37.287
Why are you telling
your parents' friend


00:56:37.448 --> 00:56:38.768
that you love him?


00:56:38.927 --> 00:56:41.175
The door's open.
What's going on?


00:56:41.327 --> 00:56:43.575
Nina, I need to talk to you.


00:56:43.727 --> 00:56:45.811
Can we go somewhere
for, like, five minutes?


00:56:45.967 --> 00:56:47.647
Ethan!
I think you should leave.


00:56:47.807 --> 00:56:50.655
- Ethan Ethan?
- Yes! Just five minutes!


00:56:50.806 --> 00:56:52.726
She said no, Ethan.


00:56:52.886 --> 00:56:55.134
I'm gonna ask you one more time
to get out of here.


00:56:55.287 --> 00:56:59.935
And if I don't, Pops,
what are you gonna do about it?


00:57:00.086 --> 00:57:01.046
Arggh!


00:57:01.205 --> 00:57:02.613
'Dad!
Hey!


00:57:02.766 --> 00:57:03.606
- David!
- Dad!


00:57:03.766 --> 00:57:05.370
Get off me!


00:57:06.806 --> 00:57:09.054
# Your eyes
are like starlight now


00:57:09.205 --> 00:57:10.733
# To break this spell


00:57:10.885 --> 00:57:13.766
# I'll take your hat
Your hair looks swell... #


00:57:13.925 --> 00:57:15.725
Why don't you go fuck...


00:57:15.885 --> 00:57:18.612
- What?
- Nothing.


00:57:18.764 --> 00:57:20.369
Its OK.


00:57:23.044 --> 00:57:27.245
# Baby,
it's cold outside. #


00:57:37.164 --> 00:57:41.092
Yes, I cheated on you.
And for that, I am deeply sorry.


00:57:41.244 --> 00:57:44.332
But here's the thing.
I'm a sabotager.


00:57:44.483 --> 00:57:48.084
See, any time
anything good happens to me,


00:57:48.243 --> 00:57:50.087
I...I...I just try
and ruin it, you know,


00:57:50.243 --> 00:57:51.803
because I get scared.


00:57:51.963 --> 00:57:55.651
Now, things with us
were really...real.


00:57:55.802 --> 00:57:58.410
But I didn't feel like
I deserved you,


00:57:58.562 --> 00:58:02.163
so I became the sabotager
and, like, destroyed it.


00:58:02.322 --> 00:58:04.286
That's great, Ethan.


00:58:04.442 --> 00:58:06.526
But we can't just go on
and pretend like everything's fine


00:58:06.682 --> 00:58:08.210
because you learned
a new term about yourself.


00:58:08.362 --> 00:58:11.931
And I don't even think
'sabotager' is a word.


00:58:12.082 --> 00:58:13.969
OK. Please allow me
to finish.


00:58:14.122 --> 00:58:17.166
See, I think
you're a sabotager also.


00:58:17.321 --> 00:58:20.365
You totally pushed for us
to get married so you could, like,


00:58:20.521 --> 00:58:22.725
prove to your parents
that, you know,


00:58:22.881 --> 00:58:24.289
you were
this responsible person.


00:58:24.441 --> 00:58:28.282
But simultaneously, you were
just trying to piss them off


00:58:28.440 --> 00:58:30.360
by marrying someone like me.


00:58:30.520 --> 00:58:32.048
I've moved on.


00:58:32.201 --> 00:58:34.524
- OK? David and I...
- David and you...


00:58:34.681 --> 00:58:39.045
He's your parents' best friend.
For Christ's sakes.


00:58:39.200 --> 00:58:42.321
I mean, what... Are you gonna move
here to New Jersey?


00:58:42.480 --> 00:58:44.728
You hate it here.


00:58:46.839 --> 00:58:48.160
We're done.


00:58:48.319 --> 00:58:50.447
OK? Go home.


00:58:50.600 --> 00:58:52.127
I only bought
a one-way ticket.


00:58:55.160 --> 00:58:57.168
Well, I'm not giving up
on us, Nina!


00:58:57.319 --> 00:58:59.600
I love you too much
for that!


00:59:02.359 --> 00:59:04.519
What?


00:59:30.997 --> 00:59:32.557
What are you doing
with my bag?


00:59:32.717 --> 00:59:34.725
Huh? Nothing.
Just getting it some air.


00:59:36.957 --> 00:59:39.118
- Give me my bag.
- No.


00:59:39.277 --> 00:59:41.480
Give me my bag!


00:59:41.637 --> 00:59:44.801
- Eat me, dick slut.
- Give me my bag, Vanessa!


00:59:44.956 --> 00:59:46.439
No, Nina!


00:59:46.596 --> 00:59:48.516
- No!
- Give me my bag!


00:59:48.676 --> 00:59:52.036
- No! No!
- Give it to me!


00:59:52.196 --> 00:59:53.517
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Give it!


00:59:53.676 --> 00:59:55.159
Oh!


01:00:30.233 --> 01:00:32.077
Oh, honey. Uh...


01:00:32.234 --> 01:00:33.914
Honey?


01:00:34.073 --> 01:00:35.993
I'm sorry, Dad.


01:00:36.153 --> 01:00:37.953
Uh...


01:00:43.512 --> 01:00:45.673
Oh...


01:00:58.672 --> 01:01:01.476
Uh, you know, leave it be.
It's a...it's a badge of honour.


01:01:01.631 --> 01:01:03.072
- You sure?
- Yeah.


01:01:03.232 --> 01:01:05.076
There's aloe on the pad
to prevent scarring.


01:01:05.231 --> 01:01:06.715
OK. Um...


01:01:06.871 --> 01:01:12.240
You know, I'm good.
I'm, uh...I'm good.


01:01:14.230 --> 01:01:16.598
I'm so sorry about
all this horrible...


01:01:17.991 --> 01:01:19.518
...stuff.


01:01:20.791 --> 01:01:22.319
I'm just...


01:01:23.671 --> 01:01:25.515
Yeah.


01:01:28.790 --> 01:01:32.478
You know,
my parents were kinda weird.


01:01:32.630 --> 01:01:35.434
That's why I'm, um...


01:01:36.790 --> 01:01:41.394
Sometimes it's really hard
to say everything you want to.


01:01:41.549 --> 01:01:43.109
You know...


01:01:44.589 --> 01:01:48.997
Your father, he loves you.


01:01:50.189 --> 01:01:53.189
Just don't let that
get confused


01:01:53.348 --> 01:01:55.596
with everything
that's happening.


01:01:59.748 --> 01:02:01.111
Life.


01:02:01.268 --> 01:02:02.588
Ooph!


